WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.400
A nullable Boolean can represent three different
states Consent can be explicitly

00:00:05.412 --> 00:00:10.950
true explicitly false or unknown because no value
was recorded Those states

00:00:10.962 --> 00:00:15.838
may have very different meanings Explicit false can
mean do not contact

00:00:16.712 --> 00:00:19.925
Unknown may mean send the record for review rather
than treating it

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:25.712
as a refusal PostgreSQL provides IS TRUE IS FALSE
and IS UNKNOWN

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:32.325
Run the example and inspect the patient whose
consent is NULL explicitly_yes

00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:38.075
and explicitly_no should both be false while
not_recorded is true This

00:00:38.088 --> 00:00:42.875
pattern is useful whenever a Boolean field
represents permission approval or verification

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:44.788
and unknown is not equivalent to no
